Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Bow Turns at Kiln Three
- Story & Context: At 58 BPM, Maarja opens on a low open fifth with an unusually long down-bow while Ewan holds one distorted baritone-guitar tonic beneath her. Callum avoids the kick entirely for the first sixteen bars, using one floor-tom strike only when the bow reaches its final third. The first Bow Hinge arrives when Maarja reverses direction; Ewan immediately shifts to a flat-second dyad, Liis opens a low stopped-flute organ pedal, and Tõnu enters with a breath-heavy bass-clarinet fundamental. Midway through, Friction Bloom drives the tagelharpa toward rough instability while both guitar and organ thin to single sustained notes. The heaviest chord appears only after the next reversal. A two-beat Kiln Rest follows, leaving amp hum and one chain sway audible.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Rusted kiln door marked 3, a dark bow drawn as a long horizontal line reversing at a red hinge mark, peat dust floating in cold work light, one heavy chain hanging motionless beside the furnace. Sparse vocal fragments: “kiln three,” “turn the stroke,” “hold through the hinge,” “now the weight.”

Track 2: Black Water Owes the Drone
- Story & Context: At 64 BPM in alternating 6/4 and 5/4 bars, Ewan begins with a chromatic sludge riff that repeatedly pulls away from Maarja’s open-string center. Drone Debt forces every excursion to collapse back into the same low fifth before the next variation can begin. Maarja uses Reverse Weight so down-bows carry full guitar and floor tom while up-bows strip the arrangement to tagelharpa, bass clarinet, and one low organ pipe. Callum drops the chain once at the end of every third repayment cycle. Tõnu uses a split-tone bass-clarinet note a minor second above the drone, increasing tension without changing the riff. The central section contains the EP’s longest Kiln Rest: nearly a full bar of room noise before the drone returns alone.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Black drainage water beside a peat conveyor, one repeated musical line bending away from and back toward a central dark-red drone mark, handwritten maintenance ledger stamped DEBT PAID, cold marsh grass beyond broken windows. Sparse vocal fragments: “black water,” “owe the drone,” “come back low,” “debt paid.”

Track 3: Furnace Cold, Hair Still Moving
- Story & Context: The closer runs at 48 BPM and begins after the amplifiers have already been switched on, so the first audible sound is hum rather than a note. Maarja performs extremely slow bow strokes on a single low string while Liis sustains one soft organ pedal and Callum uses only hand-muted floor-tom resonance. Ewan does not enter until nearly two minutes in, then adds one massive two-note baritone-guitar chord per Bow Hinge. Tõnu alternates between bass clarinet air and flatwound electric-bass fifths. In the final section, the band progressively removes amplified layers while Maarja keeps bowing. The last guitar chord fades, the organ wind stops, the chain settles, and the room becomes nearly silent. One final up-bow continues after every other instrument has ended. The EP closes on raw horsehair scrape and the natural decay of the wooden body.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Cold furnace room after shutdown, dead pressure gauges, one dark tagelharpa bow still moving under a single cream work lamp, amplifier pilot lights fading in the background, frost along a narrow industrial window. Sparse vocal fragments: “furnace cold,” “hair still moving,” “leave the amp,” “one stroke left.”

